SSH for ad-hoc ops (logs, process status, one-off checks) only when the user asks. Routine product deploys follow `after-every-change-docs-commit-deploy.mdc` (push, then pull/rebuild on the VPS). Skip deploy when the user says so, or for **this-repo meta** such as `.cursor/rules/`-only edits.

**Source of truth:** Code changes land via git push → `git pull` on the server. Do not treat live edits on the VPS as the canonical source; patch on the server only for emergency triage, then bring the fix back into git.

